+"""Mesh-adaptive acoustic FWI on the smoothed Marmousi2 window, one frequency.
+
+The window, the pad and the conforming sea floor are those of the mesh
+adaptation tests (``demos/automatic_mesh_adaptation``): 9 km to 11 km of
+Marmousi2, 1.6 km deep, 0.3 km of pad at the bottom and on both sides. The
+model that generates the data is the smoothed window
+(``marmousi_window_s250.npz``); the starting model smooths its slowness
+below the sea floor with a wider Gaussian. Six sources at 50 m depth and 101
+receivers at 100 m depth, a 5 Hz Ricker wavelet and one stage without a
+filter.
+
+The water layer is known (sea-floor depth and water velocity, as in marine
+practice): the parameter grid fixes the water above the sea floor and
+interpolates only the sediment below it, so the sea floor is a jump at its
+depth, where the meshes have an edge, and not a ramp one grid cell thick.
+The wave velocity is element-wise (the broken copy of the KMV space): a
+continuous velocity gives the nodes on the sea floor one value and ramps over
+the elements that touch it, which limits the meshes to first-order
+convergence; element-wise, each side keeps its value and the elements keep
+their high order. The data, the inversion and the audits all use it.
+The derivative is zero in the water by construction, and a gradient mask
+sets it to zero there explicitly. The misfit uses the full traces; the mesh
+audits and the noise level use the traces after the sea-floor reflection
+(``--window-delay``), the window of the mesh tests, since the direct wave and
+the sea-floor reflection depend only on the known water.
+
+``reference_data.py`` writes observed data on an existing verified mesh,
+such as the conforming acoustic reference of the mesh tests, instead of the
+mesh of ``--prepare``.
+
+Two steps::
+
+    python marmousi_fwi.py --prepare --data data_5hz.npz
+    python marmousi_fwi.py --data data_5hz.npz --strategy adjoint \\
+        --output results/adjoint_update
+    python marmousi_fwi.py --data data_5hz.npz --strategy adjoint \\
+        --fixed-mesh --output results/adjoint_fixed
+
+Options of the comparison protocol (``run_marmousi_protocol.sh``):
+
+- ``--model`` (the true model, e.g. the unsmoothed ``marmousi_window.npz``)
+  and ``--initial-model`` (a window file used as the starting model, e.g.
+  ``marmousi_window_s250.npz``, instead of the Gaussian smoothing of
+  ``--sigma``);
+- ``--sources`` and ``--receivers``, spread over the window;
+- ``--spatial``: the shots run in parallel, one ensemble member per group of
+  shots (``mpiexec -n 8 ... --spatial 1``: one process per shot);
+- ``--observed-size``: the data on a uniform reference mesh of that size
+  (conforming to the sea floor), resampled at ``--record-dt``; with
+  ``--convergence-size`` the data are also computed on a second, coarser
+  uniform mesh and the relative difference is recorded as a check of the
+  reference;
+- ``--noise-seed``, ``--discrepancy``, ``--xi``, ``--restarts``,
+  ``--dt-fraction`` and ``--misfit-window``, as in ``circle_fwi.py``;
+- ``--strategy uniform --uniform-size h``: TAO on a uniform mesh of size
+  ``h``, without designing or auditing a mesh.
+
+``--prepare`` propagates the observed data once, on a fine uniform mesh, for
+all the cases, and checks the starting model: the time shift between the
+traces of the two models must stay below half a period. Each case writes
+``report_fwi.json``, the meshes, the models and ``summary.json``.
+``--summarize`` writes ``summary.json`` again from the files of a case whose
+inversion has finished, without running it.
+
+AI assistance: implementation by Claude (Anthropic), reviewed by the author.
