+"""FWI with the wave mesh updated between blocks of TAO iterations.
+
+The inversion runs in stages (the bands of a multiscale inversion, or blocks
+of iterations of a single band). The model lives on a fixed parameter grid
+(:class:`~spyro.adaptivity.fwi_functional.ParameterGrid`) and each wave mesh
+is one :class:`~spyro.adaptivity.fwi_functional.FWIFunctional`, minimized by
+TAO's BQNLS through :func:`spyro.tools.optimization.minimize_with_tao`.
+
+An audit measures the error of the discrete operator the inversion actually
+uses: the misfit of the mesh :math:`H` at its own time step :math:`\\Delta t`,
+with its own transfer of the model and data processing :math:`B_s`, against
+the misfit of its uniform refinement :math:`h` at :math:`\\Delta t/2`. With
+:math:`d` the traces of each,
+
+.. math::
+
+    E_s = \\|B_s(d_{H,\\Delta t} - d_{h,\\Delta t/2})\\|, \\qquad
+    R_s = \\|B_s d_{H,\\Delta t} - B_s d_{obs,s}\\|, \\qquad
+    \\tau_s = \\min(\\varepsilon_{\\max} \\|B_s d_{obs,s}\\|,\\
+    \\kappa \\max(R_s, \\sigma_s)),
+
+with :math:`\\sigma_s` the noise level, and, for the step of the optimizer,
+
+.. math::
+
+    e_g = \\|P(g_H) - P(g_h)\\|_M \\le \\xi \\|P(g_H)\\|_M,
+
+with :math:`g` the gradients on the grid, :math:`P` the removal of the
+components of the active bounds and :math:`M` the lumped mass of the grid,
+the metric of BQNLS. The first criterion bounds the modelling error by a
+fraction of the residual and of the noise (the discrepancy side of iterative
+regularization); the second keeps the coarse gradient a descent direction of
+the refined problem (inexact-gradient optimization). The worst ratio,
+:math:`\\rho = \\max(\\max_s E_s/\\tau_s,\\ e_g/(\\xi\\|P g_H\\|))`, accepts a new
+mesh when :math:`\\rho \\le \\theta` and fails an audit when :math:`\\rho > 1`.
+A third solve, of the mesh at :math:`\\Delta t/2`, splits :math:`E_s` into a
+time part and a space part: a failure dominated by time halves the time step
+instead of refining the mesh.
+
+Flow:
+
+1. *Start of the inversion.* An initial phase raises the cells per
+   wavelength of a uniform mesh until the two-level pilot is reliable
+   (relative error at most ``eta_reliable``). It runs only once.
+2. *Start of each stage.* The pilot on the current mesh and model gives the
+   adjoint indicator; the audit gives the error. A new mesh is designed from
+   the indicator, with the budget predicted from the error (it may go up or
+   down), and verified by the audit, growing the budget until it is
+   accepted.
+3. *Inside a stage.* TAO runs on the accepted mesh. After each accepted
+   iterate the ratio is *predicted* from quantities TAO already has: on a
+   fixed mesh :math:`E_s` and :math:`e_g` change slowly, while
+   :math:`R_s \\approx R_s^{a}\\sqrt{J/J^{a}}` follows the misfit and the
+   gradient norm is TAO's own (superscript :math:`a`: the last audit). An
+   audit runs when the predicted ratio exceeds ``predict_threshold`` or
+   ``audit_every`` iterations have passed; a failed audit ends TAO at that
+   iterate and the mesh is refined, never coarser than the current one
+   anywhere, and verified. The mesh is coarsened only at the start of a
+   stage.
+4. *Every change of mesh or time step* starts a new TAO solve from the
+   current model: the functional and the gradient are evaluated again and
+   the quasi-Newton history restarts (BQNLS resets it at every solve).
+5. *Stopping.* With ``discrepancy`` the stage ends when the residual falls
+   to :math:`\\tau_D\\|\\sigma + E\\|` (discrepancy principle with the
+   modelling error).
+
+Mesh, time step and data processing are fixed during a line search by
+construction: each trial point of BQNLS is a solve of the functional of the
+current mesh, whose time step is stable for every model inside the bounds.
+
+The tolerance parameters (``kappa``, ``theta``, ``xi``, ``epsilon_max``, the
+noise level) are proposals to calibrate, not approved criteria.
+"""
+
